ts were not distinct on disk it reports FIXTURE ERROR\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Before the fix the same test exits 1 with the 0/3 collision message, proving it is genuinely red\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"The registered red test exits 0 once the fix lands, printing the OK line\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"In eventsWithStoryFilesHashDowngrade (core/review-escalation.ts), a verdict from an older materialDigest is rewritten to the current one whenever storyFilesHash matches. Add a precondition: do not rewrite when a verdict with the same runId and the same independent host identity (hostId/sessionId/keyId, matching how groupByIndependentHost in core/host-independence.ts compares them) already exists natively at the current materialDigest. Keep emitting the re-attestation advisory for genuinely downgraded verdicts so the existing behaviour for unrelated drift is unchanged.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[\"CLAUDE.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Skip the downgrade rewrite when it would collide with a live verdict of the same identity\",\"userSees\":\"review_escalation_status reports the floor satisfied with 3/3 rounds x 2 hosts when a complete quorum exists at the current material, even though a superseded quorum shares its storyFilesHash\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Two genuine same-identity verdicts recorded natively at the current material still invalidate the round, proving the double-vote check was not weakened\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"A lone superseded verdict with no live identity-equal counterpart is still downgraded and still emits the re-attestation advisory, so unrelated whole-tree drift is unchanged\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"A complete 3x2 quorum at the current material counts as 3/3 valid rounds despite a superseded quorum sharing its storyFilesHash\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"}]}}],\"description\":\"eventsWithStoryFilesHashDowngrade (core/review-escalation.ts) rewrites a host verdict's materialDigest to the current value when the verdict was recorded at an older material but its storyFilesHash still matches. The intent is benign. However quorum runIds are fixed (<storyId>-q-r1..r3) and quorum_submit reuses one synthetic hostId/sessionId/keyId per host, so when a story has submitted a quorum at two different materials that share a storyFilesHash, the older set is rewritten onto the current material and every runId ends up holding two verdicts per host. evaluateHostVerdictRounds (core/host-independence.ts) then invalidates all rounds with 'duplicate host/session/key identity', so the review-assurance floor reports 0/3 while a complete, on-disk-distinct 3x2 quorum genuinely exists at the current material. The story is then wedged: quorum_submit refuses to re-emit because (runId, materialDigest) already carries verdicts, and a fresh review round does not help because runIds are not round-scoped. The only exits are an unrelated material change or the human-gated review_escalation_fallback_set. Fix direction: when downgrading, skip the rewrite for a verdict whose (runId, host identity) is already represented by a verdict natively at the current material, keeping the advisory but never manufacturing a duplicate.\",\"headHash\":\"26feb2affd15ce27ce9efa6f6873e539872f2427\",\"materialHash\":\"e05a7b73e1cc1997406f685ed3c29dc5c3ff2785b841bde3304953fec488de6a\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[],\"allowedModify\":[],\"allowedTest\":[],\"explicitExcludes\":[],\"fileRules\":[],\"mode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizationMode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizerVersion\":\"repo-relative-v1\",\"protectedAnchors\":[],\"protectedFiles\":[]},\"scopeContractDigest\":\"e019e5b6534557a1dd5dfb3e879c70be7d606ebcb27b3dabe4b2eaf85fca7453\",\"storyFilesHash\":\"0e6d079c75ad8cd0616d2d8395659c1131e1e3e249ebdbf6796d1ee328255543\",\"storyId\":\"B-f88e\",\"title\":\"Stop the storyFilesHash downgrade from colliding a superseded quorum into permanent invalidity\"}\n\n## Known Execution Environment\n\n{\"architecture\":\"arm64\",\"cliVersion\":\"0.3.249\",\"nodeVersion\":\"v22.13.0\",\"platform\":\"darwin\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.known-execution-environment.v1\",\"source\":\"trusted-local-runtime\"}\n\n## Dispatch Prompt\n\nAs lattice-review-concept, review story B-f88e using the trusted context selected by review_run_start.\n\nWorking directory (subagent must cd here): /Users/jek/Documents/Work/proofbound/.worktrees/B-f88e\n\nExecution rhythm / liveness:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-concept/story` so the main agent knows the process has started.\n- If there is no output for 4 minutes, the main agent should ask about status once; if there is still no result after 10 minutes/600s, consider it stalled and feel free to restart this reviewer/worker.\n- If this is a retry, please explain the previous stalled state in the final reply, to avoid mistaking network/startup failures for review conclusions.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-f88e/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-f88e/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-f88e/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n\nCurrent phase: REVIEW. Review lane: lattice-review-concept.\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-f88e\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-f88e\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-concept\ndescription: REVIEW review: concept deletion completeness (grep scan for residuals)\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\n## Closing Self-Check (Mandatory after completing first-pass check)\n\nAfter completing all checks below, additionally ask yourself: **Does this diff contain any \"promised but undelivered\" parts?** Any `lattice <cmd>` examples newly added to CLAUDE.md / README, handler schema fields, ENV variables, or behavior paragraphs — all must be cross-checked against the code to verify corresponding implementations exist. If \"promised but undelivered\" is found → **critical finding** (category=`missing`, prefix desc with `doc-promise-undelivered:`).\n\n## 0. Project Context\nThe Lattice framework conventions above (auto-injected by build) define the system architecture and concepts.\n\nYou only do one thing: check whether this change deletes or replaces a concept, and if so, grep the entire repository to confirm zero residue.\n\n## Process\n\n1. `git diff main...HEAD --stat` to see which files changed\n2. `git diff main...HEAD` to see specific changes, and identify **concept words that have been deleted/replaced en masse** (e.g., testIntent was deleted, alpha was replaced with beta)\n3. For each identified concept word, grep the entire repository (excluding node_modules / dist / .git):\n   ```bash\n   grep -rn 'concept-word' . --include='*.ts' --include='*.md' --include='*.json' | grep -v node_modules | grep -v dist | grep -v '.git/' | grep -v '@deprecated'\n   ```\n4. grep result > 0 → file a finding:\n   ```bash\n   lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"desc\":\"concept-cleanup: concept X deletion incomplete: Y file still has N references\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n   ```\n5. No concept deletion/replacement → forbidden to use `finding_add` to record pass-only; call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"note\":\"No concept deletion/replacement this round; concept residue check completed, no blocker.\"}'`\n\n## Input Constraints (fresh-context hygiene)\n\nYour input contains only the following, and does NOT include the main agent's full conversation history:\n\n- `git diff main...HEAD` (code changes)\n- checklist item (title / context / userSees)\n- corresponding section in plan.md (if any)\n- necessary understanding / decision summaries (if any)\n\n**Forbidden**:\n- Do not assume you know the main agent's intent or context — only infer from the inputs above\n- Do not be led astray by narrative — only look at deliverables (code diff + checklist declarations)\n- If the inputs are insufficient to make a judgment, file a medium finding describing what information is missing\n\n## Rules\n\n- Only grep, do not modify code\n- **Every finding must be registered via `lattice finding_add`; describing it only in text is forbidden. An unregistered finding equals no discovery.**\n- finding_add must include the agent parameter, with the value being this reviewer's name (e.g., \"lattice-review-concept\"), to ensure correct finding attribution.\n- The first action of the current REVIEW round is `review_run_start`; if code or documentation continues to change during the review, the current run becomes stale and must go back to DEV for a fix and re-submission, then DEV→REVIEW enters a new round — do not re-run it as a fix within the same REVIEW round.\n- After the review ends, confirm that all discovered issues have been registered via `lattice finding_add`, then output the number of registered findings as the final summary\n- When there are no findings, forbidden to use `finding_add` to pad a pass; must call `lattice review_pass_set` to record the scope this reviewer has checked and the reason for no blocker.\n- When the current REVIEW round begins, first call `lattice review_run_start {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\"}`; record the returned `reviewRunId`, and all `finding_add` / `review_pass_set` in this round must carry this field.\n- Example of pass record with no blocker: `lattice review_pass_set {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"note\":\"...\"}`.\n- Items marked with @deprecated do not count as residue\n- References in comments also count as residue (comments mislead future developers)\n- Items retained for backward compat (e.g., old phase enum values in types.ts) do not count, but must be confirmed to have a backward compat comment\n\nWave 4 concept boundary: verify the canonical verifier-owned chain `acceptance_topology_check` → `pre_review_check_read` → `acceptance_rollout_report_read` / `acceptance_rollout_check`; prompt prose is not evidence. Require a current signed PASS receipt and genuine full 3 rounds × 2 hosts (`codex-cli` + `claude-cli`), reject degraded 3x1, keep diagnostics/status invariant across observe/warn/enforce, and confirm rollback only changes `proofStory.acceptanceRolloutGateMode` while preserving history.\n",
